Z||000000||Jake_Dragon||10-15-2001||06:28 PM||||Bought an 85 GT that's been lowered in the front, looks good just wondering how do I check to see how much. Could some of you that are still at stock ride height in the front give me some measurements from the center of the wheel to the top of the fender well. If there is a better way to measure let me know. Mine is riding at about 12 3/4 inches from center of wheel to top of the wheel well. Asked the previous owner and he said he bought it that way. <P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"><B>1985 GT</B></FONT><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt.GIF"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||10-15-2001||08:10 PM||||Hey Jake!<BR>Get the car up on a lift and check the front lower ball joints!<BR>Mine had that nice custom lowered look till the left front lower ball joint seperated!!!<BR>Now, with all new parts, it is back to stock ride height...<P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||10-15-2001||08:41 PM||||factory measured them from ground up to rocker panels at the rear of the front wheel and ahead of the rear wheels. If i remember right its around 7"||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake_Dragon||10-15-2001||08:53 PM||||Thanks for the input. From the measurements on my Coupe it looks like its been lowered about 2 inches, I haven't had the wheels off yet but everything feels tight. I am not driving it yet but it wont be long  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Will pull all the wheels to do the breaks and take a look at all the suspension.||||reg||1
